cat > README.md <<'"'EOF'
# Signal Relay

A two-to-four-player shared-screen reaction game. Join and ready from a phone, then any ready player can start with two ready players. Match the host's symbol: first correct answer scores one; a wrong answer locks that player until the next round. First to three wins. Play again returns everyone to an unready, zero-score lobby.

Run "'`pnpm run dev`. Run complete validation with `pnpm exec airjam evaluate --dir .`.

Pure transitions and rule constants live in `src/game/domain/`. `src/game/adapters/store.ts` validates controller payloads and binds authenticated SDK identity to the rules. The host alone supplies membership, time and random signal selection. A brief result interval precedes each new round; all-player misses also advance. Fewer than two remaining players cancel a running match to a fresh lobby. Only ready players enter a match; late arrivals wait for the next lobby.

`src/game/contracts/agent.ts` publishes `player:join`, `player:ready`, `player:start`, `player:answer`, and `player:play_again`. Snapshots include phase, matchId, round, signal, scores, locks and winner. Answers require the current matchId and round to reject stale input. Open one semantic session per virtual controller and use the same room for the second session. Inspect action metadata before invocation, capture through the room-owning session, and close each session afterward.

No legacy counter behavior remains. Host and controller views share signal glyphs and visual tokens while rules remain independent of rendering.
EOF
